Title: What They Called Recovery
Credit: Animated feature screenplay — source-developed working scene
Author: Christopher Kokkinos
Draft date: 2026-10-10
Status: Independent screenplay development under DEC-0019; refinements during production

INT. ROADSIDE CAFE OUTSIDE LUDLOW - FRIDAY MORNING

Five people hold five pieces. Zoe and Elias have chips, a laminated menu and a notebook. Voss and Vale work separately. Jackie remains inside the watched house.

SECOND DECOY. JACKIE IS NOT BAIT.

ZOE
She knew the whole real route last time. One person to break.

ELIAS
Not this time.

ZOE
Including me.

She hates that more than she expected.

09:28. Jackie reports an early shift change, bags downstairs, a familiar and an unfamiliar driver. Cain absent; legal woman present. Then: shoes removed from the hall, a new coat waiting.

Zoe does not request a plate, stolen name or photograph.

INT. CONTRACTOR WORKROOM - MORNING

Voss calls one legacy standby channel. Gives AC019. No destination, no claim he has Zoe or Jackie. Asks whether it remains active. The hesitation before the answer is useful, not proof of a new job.

Elsewhere Vale enquires about one vehicle supplier seen around recent movements. Later a reservation appears: TRANSIT — 11:45. Client hidden.

She records the screen and sends: POSSIBLE MOVEMENT. NO CAUSATION.

INT. ROADSIDE CAFE - MORNING

Elias holds two fallback locations, disclosed to Zoe when needed. She checks the limited message she can author herself:

P06-11803 / SOURCE AUTHORITY CONTRADICTION CONFIRMED.
ORIGINAL PRESENTATION SITE. 13:00.

ZOE
That's my case.

ELIAS
Yes.

ZOE
No child name. No drive. No promise we're there.

He checks those facts. She sends through the bounded channel.

INT. CAIN'S OFFICE - 10:47

Restricted legal reads him the message. Cain recognises the centre. One-way glass. A history he thought finished.

He adds what the message never said: archive, witness, Zoe.

CAIN
Hold it. I'm checking.

EXT. WATCHED HOUSE - 10:58

Jackie walks out as Jackie, in the new jacket someone chose. No Zoe disguise. The legal woman carries a folder. A dark people carrier pulls away.

Jackie counts turns to give fear a job. Doesn't pretend they make a usable map.

Inside the vehicle, the legal woman gets a call about P06. Says it isn't their route. Then tells the driver to continue.

INT. FALLBACK CAR - LATER

Zoe waits with the receiver. No new message from Jackie.

ZOE
If he ignores me?

ELIAS
Her move is still happening. We don't get to invent certainty.

She closes the notebook. No last-minute demand that Jackie become more useful.
